<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank denies fresh gold rumours.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank denies fresh gold rumours.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank denied on Wednesday that it was again active in the world bullion market, four months after it announced a 300-tonne gold disposal.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not doing anything with gold,&quot; Bert Groothof, spokesman for De Nederlandsche Bank, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Asked if the bank was active in gold swaps or other derivative transactions, he replied, &quot;Nothing&quot;.</p>
<p>Rumours have surfaced -- mainly in the New York futures market -- that the Dutch bank was again mobilizing its reserves.</p>
<p>Analysts say European central banks are keen to convert gold reserves into income earning assets ahead of the planned start of Economic and Monetary Union in 1999.</p>
<p>-- David Evans, Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
